# Secrets — .env holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Never commit it.
.env
# ...but the template must ship. The repository root ignores `.env*`, which
# catches .env.example too; this negation re-includes it, because a pattern
# in a deeper .gitignore wins over one further up.
!.env.example

# Build artifacts: the databases are regenerated by ./create_database.sh and
# ./create_database_2.sh from database/sql/ and database/sql_2/
# The trailing * also catches .duckdb.wal and hand-made .duckdb.save backups,
# which are stale the moment the schema changes and must never be committed.
*.duckdb*

# Python / tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
notebooks/__marimo__/

# Local tooling config — a machine-specific permission allow-list.
.claude/

# The instructor's working briefs. They are kept on disk as provenance but stay
# out of the repository: Part I of README.md already carries the assignment in
# the instructor's words, and these predate later changes (the reservation count
# went 2,000 -> 5,000), so a reader would meet a stale specification.
new_set_of_data_for_database.txt
questions_for_4_marimo_notebooks.txt
